  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Order Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an order form in business?\", \"a\": \"An order form is the record of what a buyer wants: the items, quantities and prices, who is buying, and how the order is paid for and delivered. Businesses use order forms to take orders without phone calls or long email threads.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an order form?\", \"a\": \"List what you sell with a price for each item, then decide what the buyer fills in. Describe both to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, and it builds the form, adds up each order, and saves it as a row.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the different types of order forms?\", \"a\": \"A purchase order comes from the buyer. A sales order comes from the seller to confirm what it will ship. Work orders assign a job, while pre-order forms take orders before stock arrives. For buyer-side approvals, use a purchase order form.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is another name for order form?\", \"a\": \"Sales order form and business order form both name the same document. The label often follows the job: an agency scoping work calls it a service order form, and a purchasing team requesting stock calls it a procurement order form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are order form templates enough to take orders online?\", \"a\": \"Not on their own. Order form templates settle the layout, but a template cannot hide a sold-out item or stop taking orders at a cutoff. A form built with Emergent handles both, with no response caps during a holiday rush.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does an online order form take payment?\", \"a\": \"Online order forms hand the card to the payment processor the seller connects on the last step, and the charge equals the total on screen. Repeat trade buyers with their own price list usually need a wholesale order form instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a free order form template?\", \"a\": \"Form builders and design sites publish free order form templates in Word and PDF. Pick one whose columns match what you sell, then change the item rows and prices. Check that it has a quantity column and a line total for each row.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a simple order form include?\", \"a\": \"Keep it to the buyer's name and contact details, one row per item with its quantity and price, and a running total. Then add the delivery or pickup choice and the way the buyer pays. A notes field catches requests such as gift wrap.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I make a free online order form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A free online order form needs only your product list and a link to share. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a form with a live URL. Card payments still carry the processor's fee on each successful charge.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does an order form example look like?\", \"a\": \"Among order form examples, a coffee roaster's is typical. It lists three beans at $16 a bag, asks whole bean or ground, and adds $5 shipping under $40. For one-off designs with artwork uploads, a custom order form fits better.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}